# `litmus` — RAG Evaluation Library Spec v2

## What This Is

A Python library that evaluates RAG systems in two steps:

```python
import litmus

# Step 1: Generate eval set from your documents
eval_set = litmus.generate(
    docs_dir="./my_docs",
    llm="gpt-4o",
    tier="medium"
)

# Step 2: Evaluate your RAG
results = litmus.evaluate(
    eval_set=eval_set,
    rag=my_rag_function
)

results.summary()
```

The developer provides:
- A directory of documents
- An LLM model string
- A tier (`"minimal"`, `"medium"`, `"exhaustive"`)
- A RAG callable

The library handles everything else.

---

## The Three Tiers

The `tier` parameter controls not just question count but the entire depth of generation, noise, scoring, and diagnostics. Each tier is a self-contained strategy — not a subset of the next.

### `tier="minimal"` — Ship today, learn something real

Based on Section 8 (MVP) of the source methodology. Designed for first eval, fast iteration, or small corpora. Runs in minutes, costs under $2 with GPT-4o.

| Dimension | What You Get |
|---|---|
| **Question count** | 40–80 (auto-scaled to corpus, floor 40) |
| **Question types** | 4: single-chunk, cross-doc, unanswerable, adversarial |
| **Noise layers** | 2: vocab mismatch (40%), clean baseline (60%) |
| **Scoring** | 9 binary questions, 3 dimensions (faithfulness, correctness, abstention) |
| **Retrieval metric** | Set recall@K only |
| **Quality checks** | Leakage filter only |
| **Report** | Terminal summary + JSON export |
| **Alternative chunk sets** | 1 per record (no discovery) |
| **Eval set validation** | None |
| **Diagnostics** | Top failure patterns only |

### `tier="medium"` — Production-grade eval

The full MVP plus expanded question types, all noise layers, and eval set self-validation. Good for ongoing regression testing. Takes 15–30 mins, costs $5–15.

| Dimension | What You Get |
|---|---|
| **Question count** | 80–200 (corpus-aware sizing, Section 7 rules) |
| **Question types** | 7: + contradiction, comparative, compound |
| **Noise layers** | 5: vocab mismatch (30%), indirect (20%), typo+fragment (15%), clean (15%), compound (10%), wrong assumption (10%) |
| **Scoring** | 9 binary questions, 3 dimensions (same as minimal but with intent coverage overlay) |
| **Retrieval metrics** | Set recall@K + chunk recall@K + MRR |
| **Quality checks** | Leakage filter + eval set self-validation (QQ, GA, GC dimensions) |
| **Report** | Terminal + JSON + HTML report with charts |
| **Alternative chunk sets** | Auto-discovery during evaluation (if RAG finds valid path not in gold) |
| **Eval set validation** | 3 dimensions: question quality, gold answer quality, gold chunk quality |
| **Diagnostics** | Failure patterns + per-noise-profile breakdown + per-question-type breakdown |

### `tier="exhaustive"` — Full diagnostic framework

Everything from the source methodology. All 9 question types, all 7 noise layers, full 5-dimension scoring with 24 binary questions, complete diagnostics including scoring health checks. For teams that need defensible numbers or are optimizing a mature RAG system. Takes 30–90 mins, costs $15–50.

| Dimension | What You Get |
|---|---|
| **Question count** | 200–600 (full corpus-aware sizing with domain coverage targets) |
| **Question types** | 9: + procedural, wrong-assumption, ambiguous |
| **Noise layers** | 7: all of the above + register variation + multi-language (if applicable) |
| **Scoring** | 24 binary questions, 5 dimensions (+ completeness, conciseness) |
| **Retrieval metrics** | Set recall@K + chunk recall@K + MRR + precision@K + gold chunk rank positions |
| **Quality checks** | Leakage + full eval set validation (all 5 QA dimensions + coverage/diversity CD1-CD7) |
| **Report** | Terminal + JSON + HTML + pandas DataFrame + CSV for human review |
| **Alternative chunk sets** | Auto-discovery + second-pass validation |
| **Eval set validation** | All 5 dimensions: QQ, GA, GC, noise realism, coverage/diversity |
| **Diagnostics** | Everything: failure patterns, yes-rate spread, phi-coefficient matrix, failure mode coverage audit, domain sparsity, scoring health dashboard |
| **Staleness detection** | Enabled — flags records referencing modified docs |
| **Contradiction detection** | Auto-detection during ingestion — finds conflicting chunk pairs |

