## Eval Set Self-Validation

Runs automatically on `eval_set.validate()`. Enabled for medium (3 dimensions) and exhaustive (all 5).

### Question Quality (QQ) — medium+
```
QQ1. Is the question unambiguous?
QQ2. Does it test a real user need, not an artificial construct?
QQ3. If noised, is it still understandable?
QQ4. Does it avoid revealing which chunk contains the answer?
QQ5. Is the difficulty label correct? (exhaustive only)
```

### Gold Answer Quality (GA) — medium+
```
GA1. Is the gold answer factually correct given the source docs?
GA2. Is it complete — covers all parts of the question?
GA3. Is it at the right level of detail?
GA4. If unanswerable, does it correctly indicate this?
GA5. Does it avoid info not present in any gold chunk?
```

### Gold Chunk Annotation Quality (GC) — medium+
```
GC1. Does at least one gold chunk set contain the needed info?
GC2. Are alternative valid chunk sets annotated? (exhaustive only)
GC3. Is each gold chunk set minimal — no extra chunks?
GC4. If labeled "cross-doc," do chunks come from separate docs?
GC5. Are chunk IDs valid and resolvable?
```

### Noise Realism (NR) — exhaustive only
```
NR1. Is the noise profile label accurate?
NR2. Is the noise level realistic (1-2 typos, not 5)?
NR3. After transformation, is the question still answerable by a human?
NR4. Does vocab mismatch actually avoid source terminology?
```

### Coverage and Diversity (CD) — exhaustive only (set-level, not per-record)
```
CD1. All question types from the taxonomy represented?
CD2. At least 10% unanswerable questions?
CD3. Every document domain has at least 10 eval records?
CD4. Noise profile distribution matches targets?
CD5. Easy/medium/hard in roughly 30/40/30?
CD6. Cross-doc at least 15%?
CD7. Contradiction at least 5%?
```

**Output:**
```python
@dataclass
class ValidationReport:
    overall_pass: bool
    flagged_records: list[FlaggedRecord]      # records that fail >1 check
    dimension_scores: dict[str, float]        # per-dimension pass rate
    coverage_report: CoverageReport | None    # exhaustive only
    recommendations: list[str]                # "12 records have weak gold answers — review"
```

